ss (98/100).","meaning":"Composite of profitability, return on capital, balance-sheet safety and cash conversion (the Fundamentals-tab Quality score).","why_useful":"A durable, high-return business compounds value; a low-quality one needs a bigger margin of safety.","why_it_can_fail":"A single composite can mask a weak component; open the Fundamentals tab for the breakdown."},{"label":"Cash conversion","value":0.98,"unit":"\u00d7","status":"good","read":"0.98\u00d7 of profit came in as operating cash (5-yr median) \u2014 well backed.","meaning":"Median of (cash from operations \u00f7 net profit) over the last 5 years.","why_useful":"Profit you can't collect as cash is fragile; >0.8\u00d7 means earnings are real cash, <0.6\u00d7 is an accrual red flag.","why_it_can_fail":"One-off working-capital swings or a capex year can distort a single ratio; the 5-yr median smooths it."},{"label":"Balance-sheet safety","value":0.0,"unit":"\u00d7 D/E","status":"good","read":"Conservatively financed (D/E 0.00\u00d7).","meaning":"Latest debt-to-equity and interest coverage (EBIT \u00f7 interest) from the balance sheet.","why_useful":"Low debt and high interest cover let a business survive a downturn; high debt amplifies trouble.","why_it_can_fail":"Off-balance-sheet leases/guarantees aren't captured; a cash-rich firm can show low D/E yet still be risky elsewhere."},{"label":"Earnings momentum","value":37.74,"unit":"% YoY","status":"good","read":"Profit up 38% YoY (latest TTM) and accelerating.","meaning":"Trailing-twelve-month net profit vs the year-ago TTM (and whether the YoY rate is rising = 'accelerating').","why_useful":"Improving, accelerating earnings tend to drive re-rating; falling profit warns of a deteriorating business.","why_it_can_fail":"TTM can be lumpy for cyclicals/one-offs; cross-check the multi-year trend on the Fundamentals tab."}]},"valuation":{"ok":true,"is_bank":false,"pe_now":14.8,"pe_percentile":2.0,"median_pe":22.6,"earnings_yield_pct":6.76,"pb":5.58,"ev_ebitda":11.42,"quality_score":98.0,"pat_cagr_5y_pct":59.8,"peg":0.25,"cheapness":{"status":"good","read":"P/E at the 2-percentile of its 10-yr range \u2014 cheap vs its own history."},"expectations":"At 14.8\u00d7 earnings for ~60% 5-yr profit CAGR, the market is paying \u22480.25\u00d7 growth (PEG). >2 = a lot already priced in; <1 = cheap if growth holds. This PEG divides TTM P/E by TRAILING 5-year annual PAT CAGR (endpoint-to-endpoint) \u2014 a time-axis mismatch vs the textbook FORWARD-EPS PEG, and one abnormal base/terminal year distorts the CAGR. A rough trailing valuation-vs-growth gauge, not a precise forward PEG.","cyclical_caveat":null,"meaning":"P/E percentile = where today's price-to-earnings sits within the stock's own last-10-yr range (low = cheap vs its past). Paired with the Quality score and 5-yr profit growth so a cheap multiple is judged against business strength, not in isolation.","why_useful":"Cheapness only matters relative to quality and growth \u2014 a low P/E on a declining or peak-cyclical business is a trap, not a bargain.","why_it_can_fail":"P/E breaks for loss-makers / one-offs; for banks use P/B not EV/EBITDA; a multiple cheap vs history can stay cheap if the business has structurally de-rated."},"ownership":{"ok":true,"na":null,"holders":{"Promoter":{"periods":["Jun 2025","Sep 2025","Dec 2025","Mar 2026","Jun 2026"],"values":[79.94,79.94,79.94,79.94,79.94],"latest_pct":79.94,"chg_1y_pp":0.0},"FII":{"periods":["Jun 2025","Sep 2025","Dec 2025","Mar 2026","Jun 2026"],"values":[2.99,3.74,2.48,2.3,1.61],"latest_pct":1.61,"chg_1y_pp":-1.38},"DII":{"periods":["Jun 2025","Sep 2025","Dec 2025","Mar 2026","Jun 2026"],"values":[7.05,3.8,3.48,3.48,3.22],"latest_pct":3.22,"chg_1y_pp":-3.83},"Public":{"periods":["Jun 2025","Sep 2025","Dec 2025","Mar 2026","Jun 2026"],"values":[10.03,12.53,14.09,14.29,15.22],"latest_pct":15.22,"chg_1y_pp":5.19}},"pledge":null,"events":[],"placeholders":[{"label":"Promoter pledge (detail)","note":"share-level pledge hi